        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 231,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 399,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 232,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57950,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 232,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 400,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 233,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57951,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 233,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are typically deep-seated, involving skeletal muscle, deep fibrous connective tissue, or deep subcutaneous fat. Most arise in the proximal extremities and limb girdles {8214255}. Less common sites include distal extremities, trunk, and head and neck (including the oral cavity) {15472660}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 401,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 234,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57952,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 234,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients present with a painless mass of variable duration, with some reporting a recent increase in size {8214255}. Imaging studies typically show a well-defined, heterogeneous fatty and myxoid lesion, deviating from the appearance of lipoma but otherwise non-distinctive {8865499}. Calcification is commonly present {15371618}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 402,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 235,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57953,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 235,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Chondroid lipoma is a rare tumour that primarily affects adult women.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 403,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 236,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57954,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 236,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 404,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 237,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57955,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 237,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Chondroid lipoma is characterized by a recurrent t(11;16)(q13;p13) chromosomal translocation that results in fusion of the <em>C11orf95</em> (11q13.1) and <em>MRTFB</em> (previous alias <em>MKL2</em>; 16p13.12) genes {20607705; 23672313}. MRTFB functions as a coactivator of the transcription factor SRF, which regulates a broad range of cellular processes such as organization of the cytoskeleton, cell migration, cell growth, and differentiation {16778073}. <em>C11orf95</em> encodes for a hypothetical protein of unknown function.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 411,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 244,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57956,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 244,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Chondroid lipomas are well delineated, with yellowish-tan, gelatinous cut surfaces suggesting a mature fat component. The tumour size ranges from 2&nbsp;to 7&nbsp;cm; those complicated by haemorrhage are usually larger {8214255}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 405,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 238,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57957,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 238,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Encapsulation and occasional lobulation may be seen. There are variable proportions of mature adipose tissue intermingled with nests and cords of small round vacuolated cells embedded in a myxoid-chondroid matrix. The small cells display a range of lipoblastic differentiation, consisting of undifferentiated bland cells with minimal cytoplasm to small univacuolated and multivacuolated lipoblasts with fat droplets scalloping bland nuclei. Cells with granular, eosinophilic cytoplasm may also be seen. PAS staining accentuates intracytoplasmic glycogen. Toluidine and Alcian blue staining at low pH indicates the presence of chondroitin sulfate. Owing to high vascularity, haemorrhage and fibrosis are common {7628841; 8214255; 7573689}; occasionally calcification or metaplastic bone formation is seen {18259746}.</p>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemistry for S100 is strongly positive in the mature fatty component, weaker in the lipoblastic elements, and usually negative in cells without apparent lipoblastic differentiation. Keratins may be detected rarely, and EMA is negative {7628841}. Ultrastructural study confirms the presence of mature fat, as well as small embryonal cells with features of lipoblasts, chondroblasts, or both. The surrounding matrix consists of a network of thin filaments, thin collagen fibres, and abundant proteoglycan particles {7628841; 7573689}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 406,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 239,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57958,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 239,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cytologically, chondroid lipoma is composed of relatively cohesive clusters of mature adipocytes and variably sized lipoblasts in a chondromyxoid matrix {10524534; 11520278}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 407,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 240,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57959,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 240,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 410,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 243,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57960,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 243,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> lobulated, circumscribed mass with variable admixture of mature adipocytes and lipoblasts embedded in a myxohyaline chondroid matrix.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 408,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 241,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57961,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 241,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 409,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 242,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57962,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 242,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Surgical excision is usually curative and local recurrences are rare.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:06:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
